WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:05.200
- [J.R.] Art is not supposed
to change the world.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.823
But art can change the
way we see the world.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.127
So now my wish is--

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:23.263
for you to stand up for
what you care about.

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:27.300
By participating in a global art project,

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:34.996
and together, we turn the world inside out.

00:00:34.996 --> 00:00:37.230
(piano music)

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:39.930
- [Announcer] They had a big
idea to change the world.

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:43.730
But they couldn't do it alone.

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:44.563
- [Woman 1] So my wish--

00:00:44.563 --> 00:00:45.396
- [Man 1] So my wish--

00:00:45.396 --> 00:00:46.459
- [Man 2] I wish--

00:00:46.459 --> 00:00:47.292
- [Man 3] So now my wish--

00:00:47.292 --> 00:00:49.113
- [French Man] And now here's my wish--

00:00:55.475 --> 00:00:56.620
- [J.R.] My name is JR.

00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:58.373
I like to call myself an artist.

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:02.960
There's two ways of
thinking about my work.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:05.480
The easy way is just I'm just papering

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:07.820
black and white images on walls.

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:10.853
But I believe my work is
about connecting people.

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:15.280
For me, it's the power of
bringing people together.

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:21.020
I went there to do art
projects with the community.

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:24.530
Now I realized the community
wanted to do art projects

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:26.120
even more than I wanted,

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:28.480
and start thinking, why don't I

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:31.030
take myself out of the
equation and let them do it.

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:34.250
So the wish was pretty simple.

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:35.880
Is you just put up a website and

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:38.660
you can send us your photo
for whatever you believe in

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:40.423
or whatever you wanna fight for.

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:44.590
We'll send you back your
photo in large format

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:46.090
wherever you are in the world.

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:52.333
Every day I seek roles,
living around the world.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:58.882
The project went much further
than the places I've been,

00:01:58.882 --> 00:02:00.970
and that shows the power of art.

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:03.793
And the photo booth
truck is the magic of it.

00:02:11.822 --> 00:02:12.770
- [Woman 2] We're a team of four

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:14.490
traveling in the photo booth truck.

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:16.683
Josh, Basel, Jaime and I.

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:23.110
- [JR] We are reusing
two of these trucks

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:25.323
to cover 30 cities around America.

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:29.610
- [Woman 2] For just a
tool for people that wanna

00:02:29.610 --> 00:02:31.493
send a positive message.

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:36.460
- [JR] Once the truck
is ready and running,

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:37.293
anyone can come, wait for the flash,

00:02:47.708 --> 00:02:52.625
touch the screen, take your
picture, type your information.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:57.880
In a matter of a minute or
so, it prints on the side

00:02:57.880 --> 00:02:59.500
three by four feet.

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:02.663
No one is used to seeing
their faces so big.

00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:09.930
The truck has this magic
about bringing photography

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:11.563
back to the print.

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:15.400
Then the posters go to the wall.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.000
We use wallpaper glue,

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.173
put them up, and that's it.

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:27.830
We printed more than
300,000 faces already,

00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:30.233
and we sent them to
more than 130 countries.

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:41.630
- [Luana] It's the people's art project.

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:43.280
We don't decide the message.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:46.830
It can be political to
bring attention to issues.

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:51.280
- [JR] I love the idea of using
photography to promote change.

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:53.644
This specific project
is to raise awareness

00:03:53.644 --> 00:03:55.183
about the Dreamers situations.

00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:00.240
- [Karina Ruiz] Inside Out is
bringing the opportunity

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:01.540
for Dreamers like myself.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:04.810
A person that came here at a young age

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:06.330
to have a better future.

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:09.373
To come out and give a face to the issue.

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:13.190
- [VIANEY PEREZ] When people drive
by and they see a lot of faces,

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:15.690
they're gonna get curious
and they're gonna wonder

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:20.993
that's the face to the issue.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:22.943
To humanize it.

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:30.530
- [JR] You do this thing
that just pasting an image

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:33.780
up there might have no impact,
but it does have an impact.

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:37.503
You cannot know when and
how, but it's worth trying.

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:44.060
It all starts with believing, right?

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:47.670
So, if you don't believe
that you can make change,

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:49.240
change will never happen.

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:53.040
Even if it's a very small
change in one person,

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:54.423
that's a positive change.

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:58.170
This is not about JR anymore,

00:04:58.170 --> 00:05:00.176
it's about everyone that believes

00:05:00.176 --> 00:05:01.853
that art can change the world.

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:07.090
I think that definitely art can change

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:08.860
the perception we have about the world.

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:11.520
And if we start seeing
the world differently,

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:14.513
maybe it's a good path to
start changing the world.

